WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.069
- With the economy in the
toilet and the climate crisis

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:05.738
about to drop a deuce, it's
time for a new solution

00:00:05.771 --> 00:00:07.540
to waste in the workplace.

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.442
I'm project manager Beth Meadows

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:11.844
and I pioneered the "Human
Litter Box".

00:00:11.877 --> 00:00:14.647
I first got the inspiration
when I noticed my cat.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.050
If he can shit next to
my desk, why can't I?

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.485
When you work in software, time
is money.

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:21.988
Optimizing our number twos makes
more time

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:23.423
for ones and zeros.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.291
People in tech are used to new
life hacks,

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:28.428
so it didn't take long
for folks to get on board.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:32.198
The average person flushes
over 24 gallons a day

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:36.302
but litter boxes are low
cost, environmentally friendly

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:39.639
and can last an entire
week without changing.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.741
Based on the popularity of the
litter box,

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:42.809
we've even experimented

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.044
with other feline
inspired workplace hacks.

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:48.581
Sun spot naps on the windowsill
are much more effective

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:50.416
than laser pointer productivity.

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:54.387
And when space is at a
premium, you can even share.

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:57.056
But it takes some practice,

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:59.092
not everyone gets a
bullseye the first time.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.760
- Can't thank you enough
for bringing me in today.

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:02.895
- Do need to go before we begin?

00:01:02.928 --> 00:01:05.798
- No, I think, I think I am all
set.

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:08.367
- Well, do you mind if I go? I
have been in meetings all day

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.535
and I really haven't had the
chance.

00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:10.369
- By all means.

00:01:10.402 --> 00:01:11.471
I will stand over here actually.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:12.439
- Oh no, you could stay.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.707
Even better, litter
makes great fertilizer.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.444
Does wonders for our office
garden.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:27.287
(exciting music)

